.TH CTPOOL_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN 3 "2026-08-02" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ctpool_shutdown_drain \- graceful shutdown
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadpool.h>

void ctpool_shutdown_drain(ctpool pool);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Tells the pool to accept no new task. It then waits for every task in
the queue, and every active task, to finish. It then joins every worker
thread. It blocks until every worker has exited.

The pool accepts no new task after this call returns. ctpool_destroy
can then free the pool struct.

A second call does no more shutdown work of its own. That holds both
for a call that follows the first one and for a call that runs at the
same time on another thread. It still blocks until the shutdown that is
already under way stops. Every caller therefore gets the same
guarantee: after the call returns, every worker thread has exited.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
pool   Thread pool handle (CTPOOL_INVALID or a stale/already-destroyed
       handle is a no-op)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Every submit function returns ccol_not_permitted after this call. The
one exception is ctpool_submit_future, which reports a failure only as
a NULL return.
The library wakes every thread that blocks in ctpool_submit on a full
bounded queue. Each of them receives ccol_not_permitted.

A call to ctpool_shutdown_drain on pool from inside a task does
nothing at all. That holds when the task runs on one of the worker
threads of pool. A call from the on_complete callback of that task is
the same. It
neither stops the pool from accepting new tasks nor joins any worker,
and it does not block. A worker thread cannot join itself. To go ahead
could therefore never wait for the thread that called to exit. It could
only wait for every other worker.

A ctpool_shutdown_immediate call can arrive while this call still
drains. That call then takes over. It discards whatever is still in the
queue at that moment, and it cancels the futures of those tasks. This
call then returns after every worker has exited.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ctpool_shutdown_immediate (3),
.BR ctpool_wait (3),
.BR ctpool_destroy (3)
